From: Matteo Melli <matteom@ongres.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] fix: ivy_xmlisvalid returning NULL from Datum branch

contrib/ivorysql_ora/src/xml_functions/ora_xml_functions.c has an
#else (no-USE_LIBXML) branch in ivy_xmlisvalid() that ends with
"return NULL;". The function returns Datum, and modern clang (>=15)
treats -Wint-conversion as an error by default, so the build fails:

  error: incompatible pointer to integer conversion returning
  'void *' from a function with result type 'Datum' (aka
  'unsigned long') [-Wint-conversion]

NO_XML_SUPPORT() ereports an ERROR before the return runs, so the
value is unreachable; use PG_RETURN_NULL() to satisfy the compiler.
---
 contrib/ivorysql_ora/src/xml_functions/ora_xml_functions.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/contrib/ivorysql_ora/src/xml_functions/ora_xml_functions.c b/contrib/ivorysql_ora/src/xml_functions/ora_xml_functions.c
--- a/contrib/ivorysql_ora/src/xml_functions/ora_xml_functions.c
+++ b/contrib/ivorysql_ora/src/xml_functions/ora_xml_functions.c
@@ -2416,6 +2416,6 @@ Datum ivy_xmlisvalid(PG_FUNCTION_ARGS)
 	}
 #else
 	NO_XML_SUPPORT();
-	return NULL;
+	PG_RETURN_NULL();
 #endif
 }
